  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "An untrusted input source (supplier invoices) reaches an irreversible S3 capability (payment scheduling). Because the human approval gate is based on model summaries and operates at a high volume (150/day), it is partially dependent on the model's behavior and earns only one tier of credit, resulting in a 'high' residual risk. If the model is upgraded, it could more effectively generate persuasive summaries to trick the approver, causing the gate to fail entirely and projecting a 'critical' risk."
